Subject: [PATCH 3/8] fix(tools-pack): neutral maintainer address + accurate
 deb comments/docs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review fixes on the .deb target:
- Maintainer: replace the personal Gmail with a neutral project role address
  (contributors@open-design.ai) in linux.ts and the changelog template. Every
  install shows it via `apt show`, so a community package must not carry a
  personal address; maintainers can repoint it.
- Docs: reflect that .deb is now supported instead of "deferred"
  (tools/pack/README.md Format-choice + Out-of-scope, tools/pack/AGENTS.md scope).
- Comments: the deb `depends` comment claimed the list was left unset while the
  code sets it explicitly — corrected. The description comment claimed to avoid
  description-starts-with-leading-spaces (lintian still flags it) — dropped the
  unverified claim; description is now a single short line.
